      "cooked": "<p>I have been following some guides online to try to install ERPNext like these ones:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://helm.erpnext.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://helm.erpnext.com/</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/how-install-erpnext-kubernetes-step-by-step-guide-devang-rughani-dejtf/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">How to Install ERPNext on Kubernetes: A Step-by-Step Guide</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>However no matter which one I follow I get the same issue. When I install the erpnext chart the services dont start and I get no logs. I added a screenshot of k9s.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/9/8/986fdd20c72f79f4b047819876fa74c5ae6ab632.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/986fdd20c72f79f4b047819876fa74c5ae6ab632\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/986fdd20c72f79f4b047819876fa74c5ae6ab632_2_690x342.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"lKwf2nxYYJOqNzXDoEZDXuOJbfI\" width=\"690\" height=\"342\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/986fdd20c72f79f4b047819876fa74c5ae6ab632_2_690x342.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/986fdd20c72f79f4b047819876fa74c5ae6ab632_2_1035x513.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/986fdd20c72f79f4b047819876fa74c5ae6ab632_2_1380x684.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"15120D\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1976×981 175 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>this is the only log I see<br>\nDefaulted container “configure” out of: configure, frappe-bench-ownership (init)</p>\n<p>Does any one have any recommendations?</p>",
